@baseUrl = https://localhost:7163/api
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@platformToken = PASTE_PLATFORM_SUPERADMIN_TOKEN_HERE

### Auth ------------------------------------------------------------

### Self-serve: register a brand-new tenant + its first Owner
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register-tenant
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantName": "Globex Support",
  "ownerEmail": "owner@globex-support.test",
  "ownerPassword": "Passw0rd!123",
  "ownerFirstName": "Gina",
  "ownerLastName": "Owner"
}

### Log in with a seeded demo user (see README for the full list)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@acme-support.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!123"
}

### Refresh an access token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN_RESPONSE"
}

### Log out (revokes the refresh token, records a TeamMember.LoggedOut audit entry)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN_RESPONSE"
}

### Owner/Admin: invite a new team member
### The invite token is emailed directly to "email" below - it is NOT
### returned in this response (see README "Activity audit trail" /
### the invite-token security note). Use a REAL address you can check if
### you've configured Smtp (see README "Outbound email"); otherwise,
### find the token in the console/log file - look for a line starting
### "OUTBOUND EMAIL to ..." right after this call.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/invite
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "new.agent@acme-support.test",
  "firstName": "New",
  "lastName": "Agent",
  "role": "Agent"
}

### Accept an invite (token from the email/log above, NOT from the invite response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/invite/accept
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "inviteToken": "PASTE_INVITE_TOKEN_HERE",
  "password": "Passw0rd!123"
}

### Team members ------------------------------------------------------

GET {{baseUrl}}/teammembers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Organizations, teams, members --------------------------------------

GET {{baseUrl}}/organizations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an organization (Owner/Admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Initech LLC"
}

### Create a team on an organization
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Operations"
}

### Create a member on an organization
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "organizationTeamId": null,
  "fullName": "Peter Gibbons",
  "email": "peter.gibbons@initech.example",
  "phone": "+1-555-0110"
}

### Merge a duplicate/typo'd member into the real one
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/members/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/merge
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002"

### Assignment rules & mailboxes -----------------------------------------

GET {{baseUrl}}/assignmentrules
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Route a whole organization to a specific agent
POST {{baseUrl}}/assignmentrules
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scopeType": "Organization",
  "scopeId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "assignedToTeamMemberId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "priorityOrder": 0
}

GET {{baseUrl}}/mailboxes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Zero-setup mailbox: omit emailAddress entirely - verified immediately,
### no DNS work needed (see README "Two ways to get a Mailbox")
POST {{baseUrl}}/mailboxes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "SendGridInboundParse",
  "isDefault": true
}

### Bring-your-own-domain mailbox: supply emailAddress - requires a real
### DNS/forwarding change on your end, then POST .../verify once it's live
POST {{baseUrl}}/mailboxes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "emailAddress": "support@your-own-domain.example",
  "provider": "SendGridInboundParse",
  "isDefault": false
}

### Verify a bring-your-own-domain mailbox (not needed for zero-setup ones)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mailboxes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Tickets ------------------------------------------------------------

### Working queue (Unverified excluded by default)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?status=New&pageNumber=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### See tickets stuck in Unverified specifically (see README "Troubleshooting"
### if a webhook-created ticket seems to be "missing" from the queue above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets?status=Unverified
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Manual ticket creation
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "Printer jammed again",
  "initialMessageBody": "The receipt printer at till 1 keeps jamming after every third sale.",
  "organizationMemberId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### Move status (Unverified -> New -> Open -> Pending <-> Open -> Resolved -> Closed)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Open",
  "note": "Started working on it"
}

### Change priority (recomputes DueAt)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/priority
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

"High"

### Reassign (Manager+)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/assignee
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"

### Escalate (Manager+)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/escalate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

true

### Reply (threads to the customer via email if org member is on file)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "direction": "Outbound",
  "body": "Thanks for the report - we're sending a technician today."
}

### Internal note (never leaves the app)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "direction": "InternalNote",
  "body": "Customer mentioned this happened twice last week too."
}

GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status-history
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### SLA management: currently breached tickets
GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/sla-breaches
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Triage: Unverified queue, Manager+ only -----------------------------

GET {{baseUrl}}/tickets/triage
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Register a brand-new sender against a brand-new organization
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/triage/register
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newOrganizationName": "Hooli Inc",
  "newOrganizationTeamName": "Support",
  "memberFullName": "Richard Hendricks"
}

### Link to an existing member (typo'd/alternate address)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/triage/link
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"

### Assign as an anonymous one-off
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/triage/anonymize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"

### Reject (spam / out of scope)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/triage/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

"Spam - unrelated marketing email"

### Reports (Manager+) --------------------------------------------------

GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/volume
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/response-times
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Inbound email webhook (public - no bearer token, secret header instead) --

### First message on a new thread -> creates a new ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/inbound-email/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-Webhook-Secret: dev-webhook-secret-do-not-use-in-production
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderEmail": "priya.kapoor@contoso.example",
  "senderName": "Priya Kapoor",
  "subject": "Checkout terminal frozen",
  "bodyHtml": "<p>Terminal 4 froze mid-transaction and won't respond.</p>",
  "messageId": "<msg-001@contoso.example>"
}

### A reply with In-Reply-To set -> appends to the same ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/inbound-email/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-Webhook-Secret: dev-webhook-secret-do-not-use-in-production
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderEmail": "priya.kapoor@contoso.example",
  "senderName": "Priya Kapoor",
  "subject": "Re: Checkout terminal frozen",
  "bodyHtml": "<p>Still frozen even after a restart.</p>",
  "messageId": "<msg-002@contoso.example>",
  "inReplyTo": "<msg-001@contoso.example>"
}

### An unrecognized sender -> Unverified ticket in the triage queue
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/inbound-email/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
X-Webhook-Secret: dev-webhook-secret-do-not-use-in-production
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderEmail": "stranger@example.com",
  "senderName": "A Stranger",
  "subject": "Do you sell parts?",
  "bodyHtml": "<p>Do you sell replacement receipt paper rolls?</p>",
  "messageId": "<msg-003@example.com>"
}

### Platform (PlatformSuperAdmin only) -----------------------------------

GET {{baseUrl}}/platform/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/platform/tenants/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/suspend
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/platform/tenants/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
